Title: The Hitchhiker's Guide to the Zombie Apocalypse
In an infinite and mostly indifferent universe, there exists a small blue planet teetering on the edge of catastrophe. Unfortunately for its inhabitants, they have not yet discovered the simple art of not panicking. One moment, humanity was debating over the best way to toast bread in space; the next, they were running from the shambling remnants of their neighbors. It turns out that while the universe is full of wonders, it is also full of things that like to bite.
The Guide, always eager to be helpful, added a new chapter titled "Surviving the Zombie Outbreak Without Losing Your Towel." Rule number one: Always know where your towel is. Rule number two: Zombies do not understand sarcasm, so witty banter is useless. Rule number three: If you find a spaceship, take it. Earth is overrated, and there are far more interesting planets where the dead stay dead. Unfortunately, not everyone reads the Guide, leading to some rather tragic and humorless ends.
Nevertheless, there are those who survive—resourceful hitchhikers who have mastered the fine art of blending in with the undead, or those who have simply outrun everyone else. The universe remains indifferent, as it always has, but the Guide remains hopeful. After all, if someone out there can figure out how to survive both hyperspace and a zombie bite, they just might have a chance at making it to the next chapter.